{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/551587-beast-the-primordial-mind-flayer-alike","id":551587,"title":"[Beast: the Primordial] Mind Flayer-alike?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-06-12T08:45:44-07:00","id":551587,"title":"[Beast: the Primordial] Mind Flayer-alike?","content":"I want a Cthulhuesque brain-eater for a Soul, From what I've skimmed so far, I should have a Namatru with a Hunger for Power. I'm thinking Unbreakable and Shadow Soul for the Atavisms, and Behold My True Form and You Must Obey as the starting Nightmares. What else do you think I'd need to flesh out my Illithid/Mind-Flayer in the making? What should his layer look like? What is he likely to do as a profession? For some reason, I keep seeing him as played by Jim Parsons (Sheldon Cooper). I'd be willing to trade out for more &quot;cosmic horror&quot;/Cthulhoid entity than strict mind-flayer, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2176,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2176-spectaculartentacular","user":"SpectacularTentacular","date":". 06-12-2015, 11:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2176-spectaculartentacular","name":"SpectacularTentacular","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2176_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T09:37:28-07:00","id":551725,"title":"","content":"While Namtaru is certainly a possibility, I think Makara is a good choice too, seeing as basically all Illithid live in the Underdark and similar places.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T10:00:50-07:00","id":551747,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/551587-beast-the-primordial-mind-flayer-alike?p=551725#post551725\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While Namtaru is certainly a possibility, I think Makara is a good choice too, seeing as basically all Illithid live in the Underdark and similar places.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, but I was also trying to spice up the underlying &quot;brain-melting Cthulhoid* horror&quot; aspect of the Illithid/Mind-Flayer. Plus, Namtaru just seem to lend themselves more to cerebral effects. Don't know why.<br /> <br /> *That's why I felt it was a good idea to give him Unbreakable, as the body is made from unusual substances, plus there's nothing like giving something your best shot, and have it look at you like, &quot;<i>Really</i>? <i>That</i>'s the best you can do?&quot; <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2176-spectaculartentacular","name":"SpectacularTentacular","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2176_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T12:42:35-07:00","id":552021,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/551587-beast-the-primordial-mind-flayer-alike?p=551725#post551725\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While Namtaru is certainly a possibility, I think Makara is a good choice too, seeing as basically all Illithid live in the Underdark and similar places.</div> </div> </div> </div> Even in the Underdark, the mind-flayers need water to stay wet all the time. <br /> <br /> I do think that the Makara are the ideal, not only because &quot;tentacle horror of the deep,&quot; but the whole sunken-knowledge as well as the grappling angle. They have a tie into consuming knowledge as it is, which tied into the mind-flayer / Great Old One mythos nicely with their forbidden-man-not-meant-to-have-knowledge. Namtaru, meanwhile, embody things that are hideously ugly and poisonous. <br /> <br /> I actually think that Collector could be good for the Hunger as well as Tyrants, since mind flayers want to collect knowledge from eating the brains. I see vast undersea libraries. As for whatever powers? The Nightmare names are all mixed up in my head, but I suggest that the direct damage one (psionic attacks) and one for mind control at least. <br /> <br /> For profession? Librarian is my knee jerk thought, followed by a professor or other academic. I keep going back to that forbidden lore bit. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T12:52:20-07:00","id":552046,"title":"","content":"As to professions:<br /> <br /> Illithids are often slavers, so perhaps something similar to that (e.g. pimp, hardnosed boss, owner of a sweatshop)<br /> <br /> They are also often keepers and hoarders of arcane secrets, so a librarian or academic could also work, maybe an archaeologist or curator?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T14:34:42-07:00","id":552184,"title":"","content":"Makara also have that nice grappling bonus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>SWTOR Referal: <a href=\"http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/414-gallus","name":"Gallus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"886"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T17:13:27-07:00","id":552373,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gallus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/551587-beast-the-primordial-mind-flayer-alike?p=552184#post552184\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Makara also have that nice grappling bonus.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, but Namatru inflict a Condition on opponents. And that Condition can come in handy. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2176-spectaculartentacular","name":"SpectacularTentacular","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2176_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T18:16:07-07:00","id":552399,"title":"","content":"I am aware, i was making the allusion to the fact that Illithid feed via grapple.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>SWTOR Referal: <a href=\"http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/414-gallus","name":"Gallus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"886"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T01:20:58-07:00","id":552715,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SpectacularTentacular</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/551587-beast-the-primordial-mind-flayer-alike#post551587\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I want a Cthulhuesque brain-eater for a Soul, From what I've skimmed so far, I should have a Namatru with a Hunger for Power. I'm thinking Unbreakable and Shadow Soul for the Atavisms, and Behold My True Form and You Must Obey as the starting Nightmares. What else do you think I'd need to flesh out my Illithid/Mind-Flayer in the making? What should his layer look like? What is he likely to do as a profession? For some reason, I keep seeing him as played by Jim Parsons (Sheldon Cooper). I'd be willing to trade out for more &quot;cosmic horror&quot;/Cthulhoid entity than strict mind-flayer, though.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Can't have a Deep One without at least some form of aquatic lair or chamber. Doesn't necessarily have to be a vast ocean, but it should be dark and moist if you're a slimy land-squid with a penchant for eating brains.<br /> <br /> When I think of a Namtaru Cthuloid, I think of Hermaeus Mora's realm from the Elder Scrolls. It's flooded with acidic water and green, misty vapors that give the environment a toxic and sickly feel to it. In addition to the tentacle faced horrors trying to mind blast you into insanity.<br /> <br /> <br /> It's true that the best choice for such a creature would probably be a Makara, but I believe I have an idea. Since the Namtaru are embody revulsion and disgust, maybe your character is a representation of TMI and shattered delusions? They could be the form of knowledge that mankind doesn't want to know, and would be appalled by it if they did. So when a human meets your character and learns their secrets, they suffer madness from their inability to cope with what they've learned.<br /> <br /> It's said the reason Cthulhu drives humans mad is because we are incapable of accepting the fact we are completely insignificant in the grand scheme of the universe. Our lives serve no greater purpose and we are totally expendable, the gods don't even realize we exist most of the time. So your character could be something along those lines.<br /> <br /> <br /> I'm sure a Hero would just love finding out their lives have no value!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 06-13-2015, 04:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T01:36:16-07:00","id":552726,"title":"","content":"It's mildly tangential, I know, but for y'all's consideration: Begotten aboleths.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T02:26:50-07:00","id":552771,"title":"","content":"How's this for an Atavism? If you eat a Mortal minor-template (or just their brain for an Illithid) you gain their supernatural merits for one day per dot of Lair you have.<br /> <br /> This would include things like the <i>Second Sight</i> Psychics and Hermetics, Cultists, and possibly even Hunter Conspiracy powers, but would not apply to people like Proximi or Ghouls.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/551587-beast-the-primordial-mind-flayer-alike?p=552726#post552726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's mildly tangential, I know, but for y'all's consideration: Begotten aboleths.</div> </div> </div> </div>Those fuckers are creepy.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}